From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/trilin-dptx: restore runtime-PM on the DP transmitter

The DP transmitter core power init/deinit had its runtime-PM calls
commented out, so the DPTX held no reference on its own SCMI POWER
genpd domain. With genpd now live (patches-7.2/0132 + 0133), the DPTX
domain is a gated domain; without a runtime-PM reference
genpd_power_off_unused() can power it off, dropping HPD and blanking
the display even when the DPU domain is held.

Restore pm_runtime_enable() + pm_runtime_get_sync() in core_power_init
and the matching pm_runtime_put_sync() + pm_runtime_disable() in
core_power_deinit so the transmitter holds its own domain. The existing
apb_clk enable/disable is preserved.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream ACPI/PM enablement for CIX Sky1]
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c
index ed2802e..2e5d41f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c
@@ -2015,8 +2015,8 @@ static int trilin_dp_core_power_init(struct trilin_dp *dp)
 	DP_DEBUG("enter");
 
 	//power on DP_CORE_PM
-	//pm_runtime_enable(dp->dev);
-	//pm_runtime_get_sync(dp->dev);
+	pm_runtime_enable(dp->dev);
+	pm_runtime_get_sync(dp->dev);
 
 	if (!IS_ERR(dp->dpsub->apb_clk))
 		clk_prepare_enable(dp->dpsub->apb_clk);
@@ -2031,8 +2031,8 @@ static int trilin_dp_core_power_deinit(struct trilin_dp *dp)
 	if (!IS_ERR(dp->dpsub->apb_clk))
 		if (__clk_is_enabled(dp->dpsub->apb_clk))
 			clk_disable_unprepare(dp->dpsub->apb_clk);
-	//pm_runtime_put_sync(dp->dev);
-	//pm_runtime_disable(dp->dev);
+	pm_runtime_put_sync(dp->dev);
+	pm_runtime_disable(dp->dev);
 	return 0;
 }
 
